From: Gilberto Conde <gilbertorconde@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: usb: qmi_wwan: add Quectel EG120K-EA

The Quectel EG120K-EA (LTE Cat.12) reports USB ID 2c7c:030b and exposes its
QMI/RMNET function on a vendor-specific ff/ff/ff interface. The same product
ID is already known to the option driver as EM060K, which claims the serial
interfaces; without a qmi_wwan entry the data interface is left unbound.

Found on the GL.iNet GL-X2000.

Signed-off-by: Gilberto Conde <gilbertorconde@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/usb/qmi_wwan.c
+++ b/drivers/net/usb/qmi_wwan.c
@@ -1090,6 +1090,7 @@ static const struct usb_device_id produc
 	{QMI_MATCH_FF_FF_FF(0x2c7c, 0x0122)},	/* Quectel RG650V */
 	{QMI_MATCH_FF_FF_FF(0x2c7c, 0x0125)},	/* Quectel EC25, EC20 R2.0  Mini PCIe */
 	{QMI_MATCH_FF_FF_FF(0x2c7c, 0x0306)},	/* Quectel EP06/EG06/EM06 */
+	{QMI_MATCH_FF_FF_FF(0x2c7c, 0x030b)},	/* Quectel EG120K-EA */
 	{QMI_MATCH_FF_FF_FF(0x2c7c, 0x0512)},	/* Quectel EG12/EM12 */
 	{QMI_MATCH_FF_FF_FF(0x2c7c, 0x0620)},	/* Quectel EM160R-GL */
 	{QMI_MATCH_FF_FF_FF(0x2c7c, 0x0800)},	/* Quectel RM500Q-GL */
